What is Composite Material Prepreg?
Composite Material Prepreg refers to pre-impregnated composite fibers where reinforcing materials like carbon, glass, or aramid fibers are combined with resin matrices (epoxy, phenolic, bismaleimide) in a semi-cured state. These materials offer superior strength-to-weight ratios compared to traditional metals, making them invaluable for applications demanding both durability and weight reduction. The aerospace sector accounts for approximately 38% of current prepreg consumption, though automotive and renewable energy applications are growing rapidly.

